    modelEssay: "The chart compares total global coffee production in millions of 60kg bags with average world market export prices per pound in US dollars between 2005 and 2025.\n\nOverall, worldwide coffee production expanded steadily throughout the two-decade timeframe. In contrast, global commodity prices exhibited pronounced volatility, peaking in 2010 and 2025.\n\nGlobal harvest volumes climbed continuously over the period. Beginning at 115 million bags in 2005, production expanded to 132 million in 2010, 148 million in 2015, and 165 million in 2020, concluding at a record 178 million bags in 2025, representing a cumulative increase of approximately 55%.\n\nExport pricing, however, fluctuated considerably. After trading at $1.10 per pound in 2005, prices surged to $1.85 in 2010 due to crop frosts, before subsiding to $1.40 in 2015 and $1.30 in 2020 amid global bumper harvests. By 2025, increased demand pushed prices to a twenty-year peak of $2.25 per pound.",
