    modelEssay: "The chart tracks annual electric passenger vehicle registrations (in units of 100,000) and public fast-charging station installations (in units of 10,000) from 2016 to 2024.\n\nOverall, both electric automobile sales and public charging infrastructure expanded dramatically, with growth accelerating into an exponential surge after 2020.\n\nIn 2016, consumer adoption of electric vehicles was nascent, with 800,000 vehicles sold globally and 40,000 public fast-charging points deployed. By 2018, sales grew to 2.0 million units, accompanied by 100,000 charging stations. Growth continued steadily through 2020, reaching 3.2 million vehicle deliveries and 180,000 public chargers.\n\nFollowing 2020, adoption expanded rapidly. Annual EV registrations more than doubled to 7.5 million in 2022 and surged to 14.0 million units by 2024, representing an over seventeen-fold increase relative to 2016. Concurrently, public charging infrastructure grew to 360,000 units in 2022 and reached 680,000 charging stations by 2024.",
