    type: "task1_academic",
    category: "Process Diagram",
    title: "Recycling Plastic Bottles into Synthetic Fleece Fibres",
    prompt: "The diagram illustrates the industrial process of transforming post-consumer plastic bottles into synthetic fleece fabric. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.",
    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_051.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The flowchart illustrates the sequential mechanical and thermal stages involved in recycling post-consumer plastic PET bottles into synthetic polyester fleece fabric.\n\nOverall, the manufacturing process comprises four principal phases: initial collection and sorting, sanitization and mechanical shredding, thermal melting and filament extrusion, and final textile spinning and weaving into wearable fleece cloth.\n\nThe cycle initiates with the gathering of discarded plastic bottles from municipal collection centers, where they are sorted by plastic composition and color. Following sorting, the bottles are thoroughly sanitized to strip labels and contaminants, after which high-speed industrial shredders pulverize the plastic bodies into uniform, miniature flakes.\n\nIn the subsequent thermal phase, the clean plastic flakes enter industrial furnaces where they are melted down into a viscous liquid polymer. This molten substance is pressurized and forced through microscopic extrusion nozzles to form continuous filament threads. Finally, these fine synthetic threads are gathered, spun into durable yarn, and knitted on automated looms into thick, insulating polyester fleece garments.",
