    category: "Process Diagram",
    title: "Portland Cement Manufacturing and Concrete Mixing",
    prompt: "The diagram shows the stages in the production of cement and how cement is subsequently used to produce concrete for construction. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.",
    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_055.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The diagram illustrates the industrial manufacturing process of Portland cement and its subsequent formulation into concrete for the construction sector.\n\nOverall, the production involves two distinct procedures: the thermal and mechanical processing of raw minerals into cement powder, followed by the proportional batching of cement with aggregates and water to produce concrete.\n\nIn the first phase of cement manufacturing, mined limestone and clay are fed into heavy crushers to produce a uniform mineral powder. This raw meal passes into a cylindrical rotating kiln where it is subjected to intense thermal roasting at approximately 1,450\u00b0C. Upon exiting the kiln, the cooled mineral clinker is combined with a small measure of gypsum and finely pulverized in a ball mill to produce bagged cement.\n\nTo manufacture concrete, the finished cement constitutes merely 15% of the total mixture. It is combined with 10% water, 25% fine sand, and a dominant 50% gravel aggregate within a rotating mixer drum, producing viscous liquid concrete ready for building foundations.",
