    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The flowchart outlines the sequential industrial stages through which discarded waste paper is recycled into new paper products.\n\nOverall, the recycling cycle transitions through mechanical sorting, chemical pulping and flotation de-inking, chemical bleaching, and mechanical roller pressing to yield finished paper rolls.\n\nThe process begins with the municipal collection of discarded newspapers, cardboard, and office documents, which are sorted into grades and passed through shredding blades. The shredded material is transferred into large industrial hydrapulpers containing hot water and mild solvents, dissolving the paper into a fibrous slurry. In the flotation de-inking chamber, surfactant chemicals and injected air bubbles adhere to ink particles, carrying them to the surface as froth for skimming.\n\nThe purified cellulose fibers are subsequently treated with eco-friendly hydrogen peroxide bleach to restore whiteness. Finally, the wet pulp is pumped onto vibrating conveyor screens, where high-pressure heated rollers squeeze out moisture and compress the interwoven fibers into continuous paper reels ready for commercial cutting.",
