    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_058.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The flowchart illustrates the sequential mechanical stages involved in the commercial extraction of cold-pressed extra virgin olive oil from freshly harvested olives.\n\nOverall, the extraction relies purely on physical and mechanical techniques without chemical additives, transitioning from cleaning and crushing to malaxation, centrifugal separation, and final bottling.\n\nThe production cycle begins in the olive grove where ripe fruit is gathered from trees and conveyed to the processing mill. Air blowers defoliate twigs and leaves before the olives undergo washing under cold water jets. Next, heavy stainless steel hammer crushers pulverize the whole olives\u2014including the pits\u2014into a coarse paste. This paste is transferred into temperature-controlled malaxation vats, where it is gently stirred for 45 minutes at under 27\u00b0C to encourage microscopic oil droplets to coalesce.\n\nThe malaxated paste is subsequently pumped into a high-speed horizontal decanter centrifuge, which separates solid husk pomace, vegetation wastewater, and golden oil by density. Finally, the raw oil is clarified through natural cellulose filters and bottled in dark UV-protective glass bottles to preserve freshness.",
