    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_059.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The diagram delineates the continuous circular lifecycle through which discarded glass containers are collected, recycled, and remanufactured into fresh bottles.\n\nOverall, glass recycling forms a 100% closed-loop system comprising consumer deposition, optical color segregation, mechanical crushing into cullet, high-temperature furnace smelting, and pneumatic blow moulding.\n\nThe cycle begins when citizens return used bottles to municipal recycling banks. Specialized trucks transport the glass to processing facilities, where optical scanners sort the containers into clear, amber, and green batches. The sorted bottles are fed through impact crushers, transforming them into small fragments known as cullet, while magnetic separators and air classifiers remove metallic bottle caps and paper labels.\n\nIn the manufacturing phase, the clean cullet is blended with virgin sand, soda ash, and limestone, reducing furnace melting temperatures. The mixture is heated to 1,500\u00b0C in gas-fired furnaces to form molten glass. Shear blades cut glowing gobs of liquid glass, which drop into automated moulds where pressurized air inflates them into brand-new bottles ready for commercial refilling.",
