    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_060.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The assembly line diagram depicts the continuous industrial workflow employed to manufacture and package dehydrated instant cup noodles in a commercial food factory.\n\nOverall, production involves four core stages: dough mixing and sheeting, continuous slitting and steam cooking, high-temperature flash-frying for preservation, and final automated cup assembly with flavor seasoning.\n\nThe manufacturing starts with silos dispensing wheat flour, salt, and alkaline water into high-capacity industrial mixers. Once kneaded, the dough passes through consecutive compression rollers that flatten it into thin continuous sheets. Rotary slitter blades cut the dough into long strands, while conveyor speed differentials gather them into characteristic wavy ribbons before they enter an enclosed steam tunnel to cook at 100\u00b0C.\n\nThe cooked noodles are then shaped into uniform round pucks and submerged in a conveyor deep-fryer filled with palm oil at 140\u00b0C. This flash-frying process rapidly evaporates internal moisture within two minutes, imparting long shelf-life. Finally, the cooled noodle cakes drop into paper cups, receive vacuum-sealed vegetable and seasoning packets, and are hermetically capped with foil lids.",
