    prompt: "The two maps compare the coastal settlement of Seaville in 1995 with the present day following tourist infrastructure redevelopment. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.",
    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_071.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The two maps illustrate the extensive urban and commercial transformation of the coastal settlement of Seaville between 1995 and the present day.\n\nOverall, Seaville underwent dramatic modernization, transitioning from a quiet, agrarian fishing hamlet into a commercialised tourist resort, characterized by hotel infrastructure and leisure facilities replacing farmlands.\n\nIn 1995, the village was predominantly rural. The northern beachfront bordered farmland and marsh in the northwest, a cluster of traditional cottages in the center, and a patch of woodland to the northeast. To the south of the central dirt road lay an active fishing harbor and fish market, flanked by open livestock grazing pastures in the southeast.\n\nAt present, nearly all rural and maritime production facilities have been repurposed. In the northwest, the farmland was replaced by a luxury hotel resort, while the cottages were converted into holiday villas. The central road was paved into an urban high street, and the northern shoreline now features a boardwalk promenade. In the south, the fishing harbor was modernized into a private yacht marina, the fish market became a seafood restaurant, and the grazing land was paved into a shopping center and car park.",
