    imageUrl: "/task1/task1_073.svg",
    suggestedTimeMinutes: 20,
    minWordCount: 150,
    modelEssay: "The two floorplans illustrate architectural modifications made to the ground floor of a central municipal library over a twenty-year period between 2004 and the present day.\n\nOverall, the interior layout underwent substantial modernization, shifting from physical book stacks and quiet reading corridors toward digital computer labs, self-service automated terminals, and casual community lounge spaces.\n\nIn 2004, the ground floor was dedicated to physical literature storage and formal administration. The northern half comprised fiction bookshelves on the west and non-fiction book stacks on the east. Centrally, a designated room contained print newspapers and journals opposite a staffed enquiry and book-borrowing counter, while large shared study desks occupied the southern sector.\n\nCurrently, the layout reflects modern digital library demands. The former non-fiction area was transformed into an interactive computer laboratory and digital hub, while e-book downloading kiosks were integrated into the fiction section. The newspaper room was replaced by a children's creative play space, and the staffed desk was reduced to compact self-service RFID checkout machines. Furthermore, the silent study tables were converted into an informal cafe and communal seating lounge.",
