    modelEssay: "The two maps compare the spatial layout of an air base in 2005 with its current redevelopment as an ecological commerce and renewable technology park.\n\nOverall, the military installation was repurposed into a commercial business hub, replacing military runways and military hangars with sustainable corporate offices, clean energy installations, and protected ecological parklands.\n\nIn 2005, the northern sector featured corrugated aircraft hangars to the west and troop barracks alongside a mess hall to the east. A wide concrete runway crossed the middle of the airfield, bordered to the south by a vast, unimproved grassy buffer zone.\n\nCurrently, the former aircraft hangars have been retrofitted into a state-of-the-art solar tech innovation center, while the old barracks were rebuilt into corporate commercial offices with an on-site cafeteria. The concrete runway was repurposed into a multi-lane landscaped boulevard with rapid bus transit. In the south, the former open grass was divided equally into an extensive solar photovoltaic array on the west and a protected wildlife wetland nature reserve on the east.",
