    modelEssay: "The two maps illustrate the urban streetscape transformation of a market town High Street between 2015 and the present day following a municipal pedestrianization scheme.\n\nOverall, vehicular traffic and kerbside vehicle parking were entirely removed from the street, transforming a congested roadway into an expansive pedestrian retail plaza featuring outdoor cafe terraces and green landscaping.\n\nIn 2015, the High Street was configured for heavy vehicular flow. Continuous rows of retail shopfronts lined the northern and southern edges of the street. Between them ran an active two-lane vehicular carriageway subject to heavy traffic noise, accompanied by a row of curbside parking bays along the southern curb.\n\nAt present, motor vehicles have been prohibited. The former asphalt roadway and parking spaces were replaced with decorative granite paving to create a continuous pedestrian promenade. The southern edge now features outdoor dining terraces, parasols, and planted trees. Furthermore, the retail facades on both sides were revitalized, with northern shops adding protective all-weather awnings and southern units transitioning into artisan cafes.",
